# Source data for the build pipeline — 406 MB, all of it re-downloadable.
# tools/build_city.py and tools/match_osm.py regenerate data/toronto.json from these.
data/raw/

# The BUILT city IS committed: the app needs it to run, and rebuilding requires a 210 MB
# shapefile download. data/toronto.json is the authoring format; data/city/ is the per-tile
# format the loader streams and data/toronto.bin is the fallback (tools/pack_city.py).
# All three ship -- GitHub Pages serves data/city/ as ordinary static files.

# Working spec / notes, not documentation.
CONTRACT.md


# The app serves data/city/ (streamed per-tile). data/toronto.json is the 76 MB authoring format
# and data/toronto.bin the 26 MB single-file fallback; both are regenerated by the pipeline:
#   python3 tools/build_city.py && python3 tools/match_osm.py && python3 tools/attach_pois.py \
#     && python3 tools/pack_city.py
# Committing them pushed the repo past GitHub's 50 MB file warning and toward its 100 MB limit.
data/toronto.json
data/toronto.bin
